    {
      "index": 8,
      "type": "answer",
      "narration": "Because biofilm, organisms embedded in a protective matrix on the channel wall, resists chemical disinfection entirely. Soaking and flushing don't remove it either. Only a brush that physically contacts the wall disrupts it. That's why brushing is specified per channel, and why omitting it has caused outbreaks.",
      "audioFile": "audio/vo/ms-cssd-15/V803/scene-8.mp3",
      "voDurationInSeconds": 21.744,
      "voDurationInFrames": 653,
      "leadFrames": 26,
      "tailFrames": 44,
      "durationInFrames": 723,
      "startFrame": 4531,
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "Because biofilm, organisms embedded in a",
          "start": 0.098,
          "end": 2.706
        },
        {
          "text": "protective matrix on the channel wall,",
          "start": 2.706,
          "end": 5.082
        },
        {
          "text": "resists chemical disinfection entirely.",
          "start": 5.134,
          "end": 7.7860000000000005
        },
        {
          "text": "Soaking and flushing don't remove it",
          "start": 8.474,
          "end": 10.373
        },
        {
          "text": "either. Only a brush that physically",
          "start": 10.373,
          "end": 13.125
        },
        {
          "text": "contacts the wall disrupts it.",
          "start": 13.125,
          "end": 15.152
        },
        {
          "text": "That's why brushing is specified per",
          "start": 15.841,
          "end": 17.764
        },
        {
          "text": "channel, and why omitting it has caused",
          "start": 17.764,
          "end": 20.156
        },
        {
          "text": "outbreaks!",
          "start": 20.156,
          "end": 21.064999999999998
        }
